00:00:13.881 --> 00:00:18.230
Since 1983, I went to Shaolin Temple,

00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:21.021
so now I'm the 34th-generation

00:00:21.021 --> 00:00:24.700
Shaolin kung fu warrior, disciple.

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:28.470
In 1998, I came to London.

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:32.580
My Shaolin experience
is more than 35 years.

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:35.893
Today I will break down
some kung fu movies.

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:41.265
When we talk about, "What do you teach

00:00:41.265 --> 00:00:42.823
when you say we teach Shaolin?"

00:00:42.823 --> 00:00:45.222
But because Shaolin is so big,

00:00:45.222 --> 00:00:47.060
people really hard to recognize

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:48.840
what Shaolin style look like.

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:49.815
Because Shaolin, you know,

00:00:49.815 --> 00:00:53.115
they have hundreds of
hundreds of different forms.

00:00:53.115 --> 00:00:54.630
And also weapons.

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:56.857
And also the training, 72 styles.

00:00:56.857 --> 00:01:01.490
If my opinion, so, it's
that Shaolin style basically

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:05.789
is kung fu and wisdom together.

00:01:05.789 --> 00:01:09.107
So it's balanced. The
mind-body spirit balanced.

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:17.270
He come here and try to fly-jump at him,

00:01:17.270 --> 00:01:21.390
then he straightaway know, he
don't need some fancy move.

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:22.950
He just lies down on the floor.

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:26.170
He give you one throw and give
you one kick. It's simple.

00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:29.050
For martial artists, useful is beautiful.

00:01:29.050 --> 00:01:31.458
Useless? You know, or fancy?

00:01:31.458 --> 00:01:34.341
No, I don't think it's beautiful.

00:01:34.341 --> 00:01:37.830
Kung fu kicks, you know,
they have many kicks.

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:40.251
We have dēng tuǐ.

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:43.150
We have chuài tuǐ,

00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:45.087
or biān tuǐ.

00:01:45.087 --> 00:01:47.498
And also we have backspin, high kick.

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:52.260
Sweep kicks have front
sweep or back sweep.

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:55.913
Also flying kicks, flying knees.

00:01:56.920 --> 00:02:01.420
So all the different types
of kicks in martial arts.

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:02.770
Punch is the same as well.

00:02:02.770 --> 00:02:07.590
Punch, they have some Chinese-named one,

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:10.010
also, they use, like, a boxing one.

00:02:10.010 --> 00:02:11.580
One is a straight punch.

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:14.163
And also you have a hook punch.

00:02:14.163 --> 00:02:16.880
And also they have a uppercut.

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:18.288
In kung fu, they're just called

00:02:18.288 --> 00:02:20.743
a zhí quán, bǎi quán, gōu quán.

00:02:20.743 --> 00:02:22.392
Also they have,

00:02:22.392 --> 00:02:25.746
another different one is like a backspin.

00:02:25.746 --> 00:02:28.813
So, when you're fighting
sometimes you do one,

00:02:28.813 --> 00:02:30.625
then you backspin, kick, punch.

00:02:30.625 --> 00:02:32.670
You do that one, you backspin.

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:36.063
Also they use here to fight.

00:02:36.063 --> 00:02:36.955
Here fight.

00:02:36.955 --> 00:02:39.480
We call it biān quán. It's like a snap.

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:42.955
Like I used one rope.

00:02:42.955 --> 00:02:46.290
Just snap like this.
So [demonstrates] this.

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:48.493
This punch is very powerful.

00:02:50.309 --> 00:02:52.517
Now, this called chuài tuǐ, side kick.

00:02:52.517 --> 00:02:57.440
Chuài tuǐ is very famous
Chinese tradition kicks.

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:02.200
Also it's Bruce Lee, I think
his favorite kick in the film.

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:04.133
This side kick has a lot of power.

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:10.440
He learned from the Wing Chun.

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:15.281
That's really representative
of all the Wing Chun styles.

00:03:15.281 --> 00:03:18.006
And he gave the Chinese name about this,

00:03:18.006 --> 00:03:19.531
